      "updated_at": "2026-09-04T18:28:42.214Z",
      "type": "state_behavior",
      "value": "Each top-level effect spawn begins in asynchronous creation mode with an empty pending-animation count; dispatch may transition to synchronous mode for selected recipes. While asynchronous mode is active, effect creation caps the counted population at 64 by removing an existing effect when necessary, increments the count for the new allocation, and records the load mode on the effect. Pending animations are then processed as a countdown stack until `efLib_AnimCount` reaches zero.",
      "disposition": "unresolved",
      "reason": "The hard live-population cap and successful-allocation count implication omit pre-allocation increment/failure behavior. Countdown completion also requires a valid nonnegative count and no reentrant changes; section mapping unverified.",
      "canonical_evidence": [
